# Audit Checklist — Pot Stack

## Invariants (must always hold)
- [ ] Σ card.ownershipWeight for a pot == 1e18 after reveal
- [ ] Every revealed card has ownershipWeight > 0
- [ ] pot.totalDeposited + entryFees == USDG held until purchase pull
- [ ] After purchase: feesOwed == protocolFee + entryFees; sweep once only
- [ ] After all claims: assetsClaimed + dust on pot == assetAmount
- [ ] Card can be claimed at most once; only by NFT owner; only when Revealed

## Access control
- [ ] Only factory pots can mint cards
- [ ] Only revealer can reveal; only pot can markClaimed
- [ ] Only assetManager can pullForPurchase / markPurchased
- [ ] purchasePulled prevents double pull
- [ ] pause on factory blocks deposits/claims

## Fee paths
- [ ] Creation fee → Treasury.depositFeeUSDG
- [ ] Entry + protocol fees → Pot.sweepFees → Treasury
- [ ] protocolFeeBps capped (factory max + pot constructor)

## Economic / game integrity
- [ ] Expected ownership ≈ deposit / totalDeposited (multiplier mean ~1.25 — document EV)
- [ ] No path zeroes a participant's claim
- [ ] Cannot reveal before purchase; cannot claim before reveal

## Ops / VRF
- [ ] VRF consumer set; keyHash + subId configured
- [ ] amountOutMinimum enforced on real router (never 0 on mainnet)
- [ ] Operators scoped; owner key in cold storage

## Test commands
```bash
cd contracts
forge test --match-path 'test/Pot*.t.sol' -vv
forge test --match-contract PotFuzzTest --fuzz-runs 500
forge test --match-contract PotInvariantTest --invariant-runs 256
../scripts/devnet-sim.sh
```
